      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00024",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Definition of terms",
      "ordinal": 24,
      "heading_path": [
        "What are thresholds?",
        "Key points and policy intent",
        "Definition of terms"
      ],
      "source_locator": "details.body",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00025",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "13. Paragraph 5 of Schedule 1 defines the following expressions used in Schedule 1 and throughout the Act:",
      "ordinal": 25,
      "heading_path": [
        "What are thresholds?",
        "Key points and policy intent",
        "Definition of terms"
      ],
      "source_locator": "details.body",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00026",
      "block_type": "table",
      "text": "Term\tDefinition\nCentral government authority\tThe Crown and each of the entities (and their successors) as specified in regulations - see columns 1 and 2 of the table in Schedule 2 to the Procurement Regulations 2024 ). (Paragraph 5 of Schedule 1 contains a regulation making power permitting an appropriate authority to specify those contracting authorities that are “central government authorities”.)\nComplete work\tA functioning structure that results from the carrying out of works.\nGPA\tThe Agreement on Government Procurement signed at Marrakesh on 15 April 1994, as amended from time to time.\nSub-central government authority\tA contracting authority which is neither (i) a central government authority, nor (ii) a private utility or a public undertaking.\nWorks\tAs defined by regulations - see activities which fall within the CPV codes listed in Schedule 3 to the Procurement Regulations 2024 . (Paragraph 5 of Schedule 1 contains a regulation making power permitting an appropriate authority to define the meaning of “works” (which is then used for the purposes of defining a “works contract”, see below).)\nWorks contract\tA contract whose main purpose is either (i) the carrying out of “works” (see definition above) under that contract (whether or not resulting in a complete work), or (ii) to facilitate the carrying out of works under a separate arrangement, where those works are intended to result in a complete work that complies with specifications set out in that contract.",
      "ordinal": 26,
      "heading_path": [
        "What are thresholds?",
        "Key points and policy intent",
        "Definition of terms"
      ],
      "source_locator": "details.body",
      "metadata": {
        "rows": [
